int new_len = (int)((const uint8_t *)sar - buf) + 4 + shasize;
if (new_len > orig_len)
    return -1;
stun_calculate_hmac(buf, (size_t)new_len - 4 - shasize, pwd, strlen((char *)pwd), new_hmac, &shasize, shatype);
```

`stun_calculate_hmac(buf, new_len - 4 - shasize, ...)` reads `new_len - 4 - shasize` bytes from `buf`. Since `new_len` is based on the attribute position within the claimed (large) length, this can read far beyond the actual buffer → out-of-bounds read.

